{"id":"kingdom","title":"Kingdom of God / of heaven","kind":"phrase","en":["kingdom of God","kingdom of heaven","kingdom of the heavens"],"la":["regnum Dei","regnum caelorum","regnum cælorum","regnum coelorum"],"gist":"The heart of Jesus' preaching. It is not a place but God's kingly rule breaking into history: already begun in Jesus' words and works, still to come in glory. Matthew mostly says 'kingdom of heaven', a reverent way of avoiding the name of God; Mark, Luke and Paul say 'kingdom of God'. Most parables begin 'the kingdom is like...'.","original":"Greek basileia tou theou / ton ouranon; behind it the Hebrew-Aramaic malkuta, God's reign.","passages":[{"ref":"Mark 1:14-15","note":"'The time is accomplished, and the kingdom of God is at hand.'"},{"ref":"Matthew 13:31-33","note":"Mustard seed and leaven."},{"ref":"Luke 17:20-21","note":"'The kingdom of God is within you' (or 'among you')."},{"ref":"Matthew 6:10","note":"'Thy kingdom come.'"},{"ref":"Daniel 2:44","note":"A kingdom that shall never be destroyed."}],"related":["son-of-man","lamb-of-god"],"total":101,"byBook":{"1CO":4,"2TH":1,"ACT":7,"COL":1,"GAL":1,"JHN":2,"LUK":32,"MAT":36,"MRK":15,"ROM":1,"WIS":1},"verses":["1CO.4.20","1CO.6.9","1CO.6.10","1CO.15.50","2TH.1.5","ACT.1.3","ACT.8.12","ACT.14.21","ACT.19.8","ACT.20.25","ACT.28.23","ACT.28.31","COL.4.11","GAL.5.21","JHN.3.3","JHN.3.5","LUK.4.43","LUK.6.20","LUK.7.28","LUK.8.1","LUK.8.10","LUK.9.2","LUK.9.11","LUK.9.27","LUK.9.60","LUK.9.62","LUK.10.9","LUK.10.11","LUK.11.20","LUK.12.31","LUK.13.18","LUK.13.20","LUK.13.28","LUK.13.29","LUK.14.15","LUK.16.16","LUK.17.20","LUK.17.21","LUK.18.16","LUK.18.17","LUK.18.24","LUK.18.25","LUK.18.29","LUK.19.11","LUK.21.31","LUK.22.16","LUK.22.18","LUK.23.51","MAT.3.2","MAT.4.17","MAT.5.3","MAT.5.10","MAT.5.19","MAT.5.20","MAT.6.33","MAT.7.21","MAT.8.11","MAT.10.7","MAT.11.11","MAT.11.12","MAT.12.28","MAT.13.11","MAT.13.24","MAT.13.31","MAT.13.33","MAT.13.44","MAT.13.45","MAT.13.47","MAT.13.52","MAT.16.19","MA